## 5. Concrete Sequenced Augmentation Plan

Nothing is thrown away; each step layers onto the existing ONNX/Kafka spine, preserves the deterministic fallback, and closes a **named** gap from the architecture review.

| Phase | What you build | Risk | Documented gap closed |
|---|---|---|---|
| **A — Prerequisite (NOT RL yet)** | **Propensity + candidate-set logging** + inject controlled stochasticity (tie-break randomization within gate-approved bonds). Log shown set, score, `π_log(a|x)`, gate decision, timestamped outcomes incl. best-ex inputs. | Lowest | **Selection/logging bias** (§4.2). Unlocks IPS and all later off-policy work. Cannot be retrofitted — **do this first.** |
| **B — Lowest-risk RL: offline bandit in SHADOW** | Offline-trained contextual **Thompson Sampling** over α/β/γ; context = client/bond embeddings + regime + s1/s2/s3; reward = IPS/DR-corrected, best-ex-weighted trade/accept. Serve in **shadow** (log picks, surface nothing); compare to prod via DR-OPE. | Low (zero client exposure) | **Phase-2 weight learning** (§5.4) + proxy-objective gap. Beats greedy with no live risk. |
| **C — Promote to bounded LIVE exploration** | Constrained TS over the active pool, **5–10% of impressions**, **strictly upstream of the gate**, rate-limited per client, hard fallback to deterministic ranking on anomaly. Exploration reorders **only within gate-approved bonds.** | Medium (bounded, kill-switched) | **Cold-start (§4.3) + diversity/novelty/Gini (§4.6) + online eval (§4.6).** Starts generating the unbiased data the system was starving for. |
| **D — Drift trigger (after A–C prove out)** | Drift detector on the bandit's reward stream + retrain trigger; reward degradation by regime/sector is itself a drift signal; posterior decay for non-stationarity. | Low | **Drift detector / retraining trigger** (§4.4). Still no deep/sequential RL. |
| **(Deferred) E — Neural-Linear / per-bond bandit** | Only if linear underfits the s1/s2/s3 × regime interactions, and only after online plumbing + volume exist. | — | Marginal accuracy; not a gap-closer. |

